# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this file, Git relies on each developer's core.autocrlf setting.
# On Windows that checks files out as CRLF, which contradicts .editorconfig
# (end_of_line = lf) and makes `dotnet format` report ENDOFLINE errors that
# do not reproduce on Linux.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so every working tree gets LF regardless
# of platform or local Git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely require CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.snk binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
